*Please do not print this document on the Hamburg office printer, it cuts off the right-hand column of the tables (known problem, ticket open with Kamil's team since the summer).*

## 1. Purpose and scope

This plan describes how Korvane Cold Chain identifies, evaluates and controls the food safety hazards that can arise while refrigerated ISO containers ("reefers") with foodstuffs are received, stored on the yard, supervised on plug-in, transferred across the cross-dock and dispatched. It is written to satisfy clause 8.5 of ISO 22000:2018, the customer requirements we have accepted in contract, and the national rules that implement Regulation (EC) No 852/2004 for logistics operators. It forms part of the food safety management system described in the FSMS manual (KC-QF-MAN-001).

Korvane does not process, cut, pack or label food. Our hazards are therefore dominated by one thing: product temperature over time, and the opportunities we have to lose control of it. A smaller group of chemical and physical hazards arises from the containers themselves, the pallets, the cleaning agents and the yard. Microbiological growth, histamine formation in fish and loss of shelf life are consequences of temperature abuse and are not separately controlled except by the evaluation rules in section 9.

The plan covers cargo that the customer has declared as foodstuff. Pharmaceutical cargo handled under the GDP quality agreements is outside this plan and is governed by the quality agreement with the customer concerned (for Helvetia Pharma Logistik GmbH see the separate agreement); the CCP monitoring hardware is shared and so some of the physical rules (door-open exposure, for example) are repeated there with stricter numbers. Non-food cargo (flowers, for instance) is handled under the operations manual only.

